## Section 1: File header and includes

```c
/**
 * @file board_ate_p4.h
 * @brief ATE ESP32-P4 board description layer.
 *
 * This file centralizes all hardware-default descriptions for the ATE
 * ESP32-P4 board: GPIO assignments, bus numbers, default parameters,
 * and capability macros.
 *
 * Usage:
 * - Driver layer: use macros as default parameters when creating drivers
 * - System layer: use BOARD_CAPS_* to determine available capabilities
 * - App layer: must NOT depend on individual GPIO/bus macros directly;
 *              use board_get_*_config() accessors instead
 *
 * To adapt this file to a new board revision, modify the macro values
 * while keeping all symbol names unchanged.
 */

#pragma once

#include <stdbool.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include "driver/gpio.h"
#include "driver/uart.h"
#include "esp_err.h"

#ifdef __cplusplus
extern "C" {
#endif
```

---

## Section 2: Board identification

```c
/*===========================================================================
 * Board Identification
 *===========================================================================*/

/** @brief Human-readable board name string */
#define BOARD_NAME                      "ATE_ESP32_P4"

/** @brief Numeric board identifier, usable in preprocessor conditionals */
#define BOARD_ATE_P4                    1

/** @brief Hardware revision — major */
#define BOARD_HW_REV_MAJOR              1

/** @brief Hardware revision — minor */
#define BOARD_HW_REV_MINOR              0
```

---

## Section 3: Capability macros

These macros describe what this PCB physically supports.
They do NOT indicate whether a driver is currently started.
They do NOT indicate whether the application has enabled a feature.

```c
/*===========================================================================
 * Capability Macros (BOARD_CAPS_*)
 * 1 = hardware present on this PCB
 * 0 = hardware not present
 *===========================================================================*/

#define BOARD_CAPS_LCD                  1   /**< LCD display present */
#define BOARD_CAPS_TOUCH                1   /**< Touch controller present */
#define BOARD_CAPS_STATUS_LED           1   /**< RGB status LED present */
